<article class="env-lemma" id="077R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/077R">Lemma <span data-tag="077R">39.14.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid scheme over $S$. The category of quasi-coherent modules on $(U, R, s, t, c)$ has colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $i \mapsto (\mathcal{F}_ i, \alpha _ i)$ be a diagram over the index category $\mathcal{I}$. We can form the colimit $\mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathcal{F}_ i$ which is a quasi-coherent sheaf on $U$, see Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/01LA" data-tag="01LA">26.24</a>. Since colimits commute with pullback we see that $s^*\mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits s^*\mathcal{F}_ i$ and similarly $t^*\mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits t^*\mathcal{F}_ i$. Hence we can set $\alpha = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \alpha _ i$. We omit the proof that $(\mathcal{F}, \alpha )$ is the colimit of the diagram in the category of quasi-coherent modules on $(U, R, s, t, c)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>